{"content":"{
  "now": "Applied AI Builder — agents, automation, adoption, and the systems underneath",
  "contact": "Bath / Bristol, UK · twinthos.com · github.com/twinthos",
  "summary": [
    "I build and test AI systems end to end. Not chat interfaces — agents with a written job spec, a defined decision boundary, an audit trail, and a human sign-off before anything consequential ships. I have been building and working in AI since 2020, moving between models, terminals, CLIs, and cloud environments to find what actually works. My depth comes from developing, breaking, and fixing real systems, not from prompting a consumer product."
  ],
  "stats": [
    ["Since 2020", "Building and working in AI"],
    ["Bespoke AI", "Agents for specific use cases"],
    ["Technical depth, clear teaching", "Explaining AI to non-technical audiences"]
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Current AI work",
      "roles": [
        {
          "org": "Twinthos",
          "meta": "Founder | AI agents and workflow development | Present",
          "bullets": [
            "Build and run bespoke AI agents for specific use cases. Define the task, context, tools and operating rules; test the workflow and refine it when the results fall short.",
            "Use terminals and command-line interfaces (CLIs) confidently to configure, run and troubleshoot agents across cloud computers and virtual private servers (VPS).",
            "Develop websites, including twinthos.com, and agent workflows using AI-assisted coding. Use Claude and ChatGPT to develop projects, investigate errors and test changes.",
            "Build company and project knowledge systems that bring processes, responsibilities and information together. Map how work moves between people and tools so teams can understand dependencies, spot delays and decide where AI can help.",
            "Create reports and analysis for teams, projects and ideas. Run AI simulation models to compare scenarios and test assumptions about possible outcomes for products and projects.",
            "Apply AI security auditing to agent workflows, reviewing data access and automated actions. Define operating boundaries and keep human review around decisions that need it."
          ]
        },
        {
          "org": "Humanitai CIC",
          "meta": "Director | AI education and digital inclusion | December 2025 – present",
          "bullets": [
            "Community interest company teaching AI safety, digital inclusion, and practical AI for health and everyday life.",
            "Built a key-free UK grant scraper with weekly capture across four funding bodies, delivering verified opportunities to the community.",
            "Self-hosted OSINT forecast system: free, open-source community forecasting using open intelligence and free LLMs."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Communication, education and commercial experience",
      "roles": [
        {
          "org": "Online education community on Skool",
          "meta": "Owner and Educator | More than 2,000 students at peak",
          "bullets": [
            "Designed every course in an online learning community focused on knowledge, health and vitality. Turned complex ideas into clear educational material people could engage with.",
            "Used gamification, practical learning activities and community discussion to encourage participation. Bring that experience in teaching and engagement to helping colleagues adopt AI."
          ]
        },
        {
          "org": "Humanarchitect",
          "meta": "Founder and Content Creator | 2013–2024",
          "bullets": [
            "Built an Instagram channel to 500,000 followers and around 20 million monthly views at peak through daily organic content on education and mindset.",
            "Created topics, hooks and narratives that connected with the audience. Combined educational storytelling, brand positioning and campaign content to promote digital products.",
            "Sold the Instagram account to Jason van Blerk of The Human Garage in late 2024 to focus fully on AI.",
            "Wrote six books under a pen name, developing and organising complex ideas into long-form writing."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "How I develop my AI practice",
      "caps": [
        ["LLMs and development", "Practical understanding of context, prompting, tool use, memory and model limitations. Use structured instructions, iterative testing and critical review to improve the systems I build."],
        ["Learning through testing", "Follow model releases, agent tools and security developments, then test their relevance to real work. Compare capability, output quality and cost. I enjoy finding out why something fails and working through it until the result improves."]
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "What I would bring to this role",
      "caps": [
        ["Hands-on AI building", "An educator's ability to explain it and a founder's habit of taking responsibility for the outcome. I connect the technical detail with the way people actually work: understanding the problem, building a useful response and helping others use it."]
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Initial recommendations",
      "caps": [
        ["Start with a real task", "Listen to colleagues' concerns and identify a recurring task. Run a short, practical session using an approved tool such as Copilot, with time for questions and hands-on practice."],
        ["Build confidence through a pilot", "Trial meeting notes to actions or a draft project update using approved data and human review. Provide a simple prompt guide, gather feedback and measure repeat use, time saved and corrections before expanding."]
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Tools and capabilities",
      "text": "Claude · ChatGPT · DeepSeek · Hermes Agent · Nous Portal\nTerminals and CLIs · Cloud computers and VPS · AI-assisted coding\nBespoke agents · Company knowledge systems · Website development\nProcess mapping · AI security auditing · Simulation models · Reports and analysis"
    }
  ]
}
